# Security & supply-chain engineering anchor

Apply to security-sensitive code and dependency, secret, authentication, authorization, trust-boundary, CI/build, container, outbound-network, upload, webhook, or supply-chain changes.

## Hard invariants

- Least privilege, secure defaults, explicit trust boundaries, fail closed.
- Authentication never substitutes for authorization.
- User/tenant/resource authorization is checked on the concrete operation.
- External input and external content are untrusted.
- Secrets, credentials, auth headers, cookies, and tokens must not enter source or normal telemetry.
- SQL/command/path/SSRF boundaries require deterministic validation.
- Bound resource consumption and externally controlled fan-out.
- Dependency/build-script/proc-macro changes are supply-chain changes.
- Do not invent cryptography or security protocols.

